<title>MEXICO: Camesa creates reserves for buyback.</title>
<headline>Camesa creates reserves for buyback.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican steel cable manufacturer Grupo Industrial Camesa S.A. de C.V. said on Tuesday it will create reserves of up to 250 million pesos to be charged against earnings in order to buy back shares it lists on the Mexican Stock Exchange (BMV).</p>
<p>Camesa added in a report to the BMV that the buyback would decrease shareholding equity by 80 million pesos per financial year.</p>
<p>((--Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9562))</p>
